4. Powers and functions of the University.―The University shall have the following powers and functions:―

(a) to provide for instruction in such branches of learning as it may deem fit and to make provisions for teaching, research and development of technologies and for the advancement and dissemination of knowledge in such other fields or branches of study as the Board of Governors may determine;

(b) to make provisions for research and other services for the advancement and dissemination of knowledge in such a manner as it may determine;

(c) to institute programs for the exchange of students and teachers between the University and Higher Education Institutes inside as well as outside Pakistan;

(d) to prescribe courses of studies in health, sciences, emerging technologies and such other branches of learning as the university may determine;

(e) to select, admit, teach, and examine students;

(f) to hold examinations and confer on or award degrees, diplomas, certificates, and other academic distinctions to and on persons who have passed its examinations under prescribed conditions;

(g) to confer honorary degrees and distinctions on approved persons in the manner prescribed;

(h) to enter into agreements, contracts and arrangements with universities, organizations, institutions, bodies, and individuals for the purpose of carrying out functions and activities in Pakistan or abroad;

(i) to establish faculties, teaching departments, campuses, colleges, institutes, museums, and other centers of learning for the development of teaching and research and to make such arrangements for their maintenance, management and administration as it may prescribe;

(j) to institute Professorship, Associate Professorship, Assistant Professorship, Lectureship, and any other posts and to appoint person thereto;

(k) to provide and support the academic developments for the faculty of the University;

(1) to decide teaching methods and strategies to ensure the most effective educational and training programs;

(m) to institute and award fellowships, scholarships, exhibitions, bursaries, medals, and prizes under prescribed conditions;

(n) to create posts for teaching, research, administration, and other related functions and to appoint persons thereto;

(o) to receive and manage property transferred and grants, bequests, trusts, gifts, donations, endowment, and other contributions made to it, and invest any funds representing such property, grants, bequests, trusts, gifts, donations, endowments, or contributions. To convert one kind of property into another, in such a manner as it may deem tit;

(p) to develop and implement fund raising plans;

(q) to demand and receive fees and other charges as it lay determine;

(r) to appoint members of various bodies and committees, as the Board may determine, for academic, administrative, and co-curricular activities;

(s) to appoint such officers and members of the staff as necessary and prescribe terms and conditions and powers and duties of such officers and staff;

(t) to establish and support teaching hospitals;

(u) to supervise and control the discipline of the students of the University and to promote extra-curricular and recreational activities of students and to make arrangements for promoting their health;

(v) to provide career counseling and job search services to its students and alumni;

(w) to maintain linkages with alumni; and

(x) to do all such other acts and things as may be requisite to further the objectives of the University as a place of promotion of education, learning and research.

